    "title": "Where to watch Iowa women's basketball vs Illinois: TV channel, time",
    "text": "Updated March 6, 2026, 5:44 p.m. CTAs No. 9 Iowa women's basketball (24-5, 15-3 Big Ten) begins its 2026 Big Ten Tournament play following a double-bye as the field's second seed, the Hawkeyes will take on 10th-seeded Illinois (21-10, 9-9 Big Ten) Friday night at Gainbridge Fieldhouse in Indianapolis, Indiana.Iowa's double-bye is a result of its outstanding Big Ten regular season, which was capped by a six-game winning streak. The Hawkeyes last game was a 81-52 rout of Wisconsin from Madison on March 1.The Hawkeyes are led offensively by sophomore center Ava Heiden's 17.6 points per game on 65.1% shooting. The 6-foot-4 native of Sherwood, Oregon, recorded a team-leading nine double-doubles and earned unanimous selection by the coaches and media as All-Big Tenfirst-team honors.Watch Iowa vs. IllinoisIllinois enters Friday's game after defeating Wisconsin, 82-70, on March 4 and Michigan State, 71-69, on March 5.The Fighting Illini are led offensively by sophomore forward Berry Wallace, who averages 18.9 points per game on 48.5% shooting, followed by freshman forward Cearah Parchment's 13.8 points per game on 51.1% shooting. It's worth noting the Fighting Illini's top scoring duo found plenty of success in their Feb. 26 meeting with the Hawkeyes.As the tip nears, here's where and when Hawkeyes fans can watch Iowa women's basketball take on Illinois:How to watch Iowa women's basketball vs. IllinoisStreaming: Big Ten NetworkTipoff Time: 5:30 p.m. CTSloane Martin, Christy Winters Scott and Elise Woodward will be on the call for Friday's game between Iowa women's basketball and Illinois from their booth at Gainbridge Fieldhouse in Indianapolis, Indiana, with the game being carried on the Big Ten Network.How to stream Iowa women's basketball vs. IllinoisStreaming: FuboHawkeye fans can stream the Big Ten clash between Iowa women's basketball and Illinois via Fubo, which offers a free trial to first-time subscribers.Hawkeye Radio NetworkRadio: Hawkeye Radio NetworkIowa fans can also tune in to play-by-play voice Rob Brooks and color analyst Kathryn Reynolds on the Hawkeye Radio Network.Series historyIowa leads the all-time series, 62-21.The Hawkeyes have won nine out of the last 11 meetings with the Fighting Illini, including an 82-78 victory at Carver-Hawkeye Arena on Feb. 26.Iowa women's basketball scheduleAll times CTNov. 3 vs. Southern: Iowa 86, Southern 51Nov. 9 vs. Evansville: Iowa 119, Evansville 43Nov. 13 vs. Drake: Iowa 100, Drake 58Nov. 16 at Northern Iowa: Iowa 74, UNI 41Nov. 20 vs. Baylor (WBCA Showcase in Orlando): Iowa 57, Baylor 52Nov. 22 vs. Miami (WBCA Showcase in Orlando): Iowa 64, Miami 61Nov. 26 vs. Western Illinois: Iowa 86, Western Illinois 69Nov. 30 vs. Fairfield: Iowa 86, Fairfield 72Dec. 6 at Rutgers: Iowa 79, Rutgers 36Dec. 10 at Iowa State: Iowa State 74, Iowa 69Dec. 13 vs. Lindenwood: Iowa 102, Lindenwood 68Dec. 20 vs. UConn (Champions Classic): UConn 90, Iowa 64Dec. 28 vs. Penn State: Iowa 99, Penn State 76Jan. 1 vs. Nebraska: Iowa 86, Nebraska 76Jan. 5 at Northwestern: Iowa 67, Northwestern 58Jan. 11 at Indiana: Iowa 56, Indiana 53Jan. 15 vs. Oregon: Iowa 74, Oregon 66Jan. 18 vs. Michigan State: Iowa 75, Michigan State 68Jan. 22 at Maryland: Iowa 85, Maryland 78 (OT)Jan. 25 vs. Ohio State: Iowa 91, Ohio State 70Jan. 29 at USC: USC 81, Iowa 69Feb. 1 at UCLA: UCLA 88, Iowa 65Feb. 5 vs. Minnesota: Minnesota 91, Iowa 85Feb. 11 vs. Washington: Iowa 65, Washington 56Feb. 16 at Nebraska: Iowa 80, Nebraska 67Feb. 19 at Purdue: Iowa 83, Purdue 74Feb. 22 vs. Michigan: Iowa 62, Michigan 44Feb. 26 vs. Illinois: Iowa 82, Illinois 78March 1 at Wisconsin: Iowa 81, Wisconsin 52March 6 vs. Illinois (Big Ten Tournament): Big Ten Network, 5:30 p.m.Contact/Follow us @HawkeyesWire on X (formerly Twitter) and like our page on Facebook to follow ongoing coverage of Iowa news, notes, and opinions. Follow Scout on X: @SpringgateNews",
